Reason: FLUDD held in view (api->held_fludd, zzzzzzz-held-fludd): while a first-person mod holds FLUDD in view, Mario's back flip and side flip are animated as a double jump (his body does not turn over in front of the view). The jumps themselves are as ever. Without FLUDD held, nothing changes.

--- a/src/Player/MarioDraw.cpp
+++ b/src/Player/MarioDraw.cpp
@@ -1078,8 +1078,18 @@
 	}
 }
 
+#ifdef TARGET_PC
+// FLUDD held in view: the back flip's and side flip's animations as a double jump's
+// (ext/modapi/game/modapi_held_fludd.cpp)
+bool PortFluddHeldNoFlip(TMario* mario, int anm_id);
+#endif
